{"availability":"available","full":"SalCyberAware/SOCTriage","name":"SOCTriage","description":"AI-powered SOC alert triage assistant, enrichment, MITRE ATT&CK mapping, incident reports, case management, and playbooks for cybersecurity analysts","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-02T22:39:51Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:21:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://soctriage.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://soctriage.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.859Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.859Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.859Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.859Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AI-powered SOC alert triage assistant. A free, open-source alternative to enterprise SOAR platforms.","[]( []( []( []( []( []( []( []( [](LICENSE) [](","No key material, and no free text: not rawalert, not analyst notes, not note bodies, not resolution text. The actor is named by a short hash prefix, never by the key or the session token, and audit.buildentry refuses an actorid that is not lowercase hex of exactly that length. The entry records that a change happened. What it said belongs to the case timeline, which is already persisted and already served by GET /api/cases/{id}."],"features":["IOC Enrichment. Queries 11 threat intelligence engines via ThreatScan and returns aggregated verdicts and threat scores","AI Incident Reports. Claude AI generates executive summaries, threat classifications, affected asset identification, and recommended actions","MITRE ATT&CK Mapping. Every IOC is automatically mapped to relevant ATT&CK techniques and tactics with direct links to attack.mitre.org","Severity Scoring. LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH / CRITICAL based on weighted engine results, on a 0 to 100 scale","Response Playbook. Step-by-step containment, investigation, eradication, and recovery guidance tailored to the specific threat"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"16cafcd3ac679af2fabe687d27bf09529f31f3bf66bb4926b348b2f89a680178","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:12.021Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:12.021Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"AI-powered SOC alert triage assistant. A free, open-source alternative to enterprise SOAR platforms.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Use TheHive + Cortex when you want full self-hosted control over case data, have the ops capacity to run Elasticsearch/Cassandra, and prefer composing analyzers yourself.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"[token] needs an X-Session-Token. [scoped] returns only the cases that token opened, or every case with a valid X-API-Key. [owner or key] needs the token that opened the case, or the key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"An operator who needs every case types the key into the Admin API key field at the bottom of the page.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"If you self-host against a different API origin, add it to connect-src there.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"16cafcd3ac679af2fabe687d27bf09529f31f3bf66bb4926b348b2f89a680178","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:12.021Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T21:21:02Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SalCyberAware/SOCTriage/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026